==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|cel-gau|la}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*beu||swelling}}, same source as Middle Dutch {{m|dum|puyl||bag}} and Lithuanian {{m|lt|bule||buttocks}}.<ref>Skeat, An Etymological Dictionary of the English Language</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-pronunc|bulla}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|bulla||bullae|f|first}}

# a [[bubble]], a water bubble; any round object that has swollen
# {{label|la|on a door etc.}} a [[boss]], a [[knob]]
# the {{l|en|bulla}}, an amulet worn upon the neck
# {{label|la|Ecclesiastical Latin}} handwritten document from the pope or the papal chancellery ([[papal bull]])

====Derived terms====
* [[bulla dignus|bullā dignus]] (childish)

